<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    angr test_decompiling_missing_function_call (binary `adams`, function `main`,
    x86-64 GCC PIE).  main's getopt() dispatch is a textbook GCC PIC jump table:

        idx = m - 0x3f ; sub 0x36 ; ja DEFAULT     (range guard, idx LEu 0x36)
        idx spilled to the stack, reloaded for the table load
        movslq (table + idx*4) ; add table_base ; jmp   (table at 0x96ac, 55
        self-relative entries)

    kuna's jump-table recovery runs early on the partial/truncated function,
    before the `sub;ja` flag idiom is simplified and before the stack spill is
    collapsed, so JumpBasic::analyzeGuards cannot bound the index.  The basic
    model is declined, JumpTable::recoverAddresses throws "Too many branches",
    and FlowInfo::truncateIndirectJump rewrites the BRANCHIND into a CALLIND
    (the "Treating indirect jump as call" marker)  -  collapsing the whole switch
    AND the surrounding getopt loop into one bogus computed call.  angr recovers
    the switch (6 cases plus default); the test asserts the call to fileno() and
    the -e/strdup case do not go missing.

    Stage model: S2 "switch-model" sub-stage.  The kuna gate `option
    switchguardbound on` makes JumpBasic::recoverModel, after the normal model
    (and the modulo/and-mask extension) fail to bound the table, EVALUATE the
    range guard as a function of the index and re-bound the table to [0, N).  The
    boundary case 0x36 (m == 0x75, 'u'/userlist) requires N == 0x37 (55), proving
    the bound merges the simplified `idx GT 0x35 and m != 0x75` form, not just the
    naive `idx LT 0x36`.  Default OFF (opt-in; the heuristic asserts a value
    correspondence across a memory spill it cannot prove in dataflow).

    Only main is decompiled.  main's code (0x8e40, 880 bytes) and the read-only
    jump table (0x96ac, 55 4-byte entries) are embedded; the case targets are all
    inside main.  Callees are named to bound main's flow; data refs render dat_.

    Pass 1 (option switchguardbound off): the bug  -  no switch, the BRANCHIND
    renders as a computed (code *) call.
    Pass 2 (option switchguardbound on): the fix  -  a single switch with the
    recovered getopt case labels (including the boundary case 0x36) plus default.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x8e40">

</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x96ac">

</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x8e40" name="main"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x8e00" name="usage"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x91b0" name="assert_execution_on_testbed"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x8d40" name="accept_loop"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x8770" name="read_loop"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x2490" name="setup_socket"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x2290" name="ingest_emaillist"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option switchguardbound off</com>
  <com>lo fu main</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option switchguardbound on</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="angr-missing-function-call #1: fix recovers a switch (none in pass 1 off, one in pass 2 on)" min="1" max="1">switch\(</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="angr-missing-function-call #2: bug renders the unrecovered jump as a computed call (pass 1 off only)" min="1" max="1">\(code \*\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="angr-missing-function-call #3: boundary case 0x36 (u/userlist) recovered, proving bound N==0x37 not 0x36" min="1" max="1">case 0x36:</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="angr-missing-function-call #4: case 0x26 (e/emaillist) recovered" min="1" max="1">case 0x26:</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="angr-missing-function-call #5: case 0x2e (m/maillist) recovered" min="1" max="1">case 0x2e:</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
